cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MaudeDash: an open analytic platform for the FDA MAUDE medical device adverse event database"
message: "If you use MaudeDash in research, please cite both the software and the paper below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Porwal
    given-names: Mokshal
    website: "https://mokshalmedia.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mokshalstudios/MAUDE-DASH"
url: "https://maudedash.com"
abstract: >-
  MaudeDash provides publication-grade analytics over the United States Food and
  Drug Administration Manufacturer and User Facility Device Experience (MAUDE)
  database. It classifies patient outcomes using the seven harm categories
  defined at 21 CFR 803.3, reports proportions with Wilson score confidence
  intervals, screens for disproportionality using the proportional reporting
  ratio and reporting odds ratio under the EMA 2008 criteria, tests temporal
  trends with the Cochran-Armitage and Mann-Kendall tests, and generates a
  STROBE-style methods paragraph matching the analysed cohort. It ships in two
  tiers: a static browser application that queries a Parquet extract of the full
  20.7-million-report corpus using DuckDB-WASM with no server-side process, and
  a Streamlit research edition that runs against a locally built DuckDB
  containing the complete corpus with untruncated narratives.
keywords:
  - MAUDE
  - medical device safety
  - pharmacovigilance
  - post-market surveillance
  - adverse event reporting
  - disproportionality analysis
  - signal detection
  - FDA
license: MIT
version: "5.0"
